// The re-export chain's consumer: the middle package of the chain (its
// own ds source is not part of this example) holds one row —
//
//   pub import @deep (base, base as origin, step, unit)
//
// so the origin package's callable, const, and struct join the middle
// package's export surface under the names the row bound, and this
// entry selects them beside the middle package's own `twice` through
// one import row. A chain needs declared deps: the origin and middle
// packages install with `ds save`, the entry's ds.pkg declares the
// middle package, and `ds run` over the package root serves the chain
// — a plain script run of this file declares no deps, so the names
// stay unbound. The CLI example gate stages exactly that tree and runs
// this file as the root package's entry.

import @std/io
import @lib (twice, base, origin, step, unit)

fn main() -> int {
  println("hi")
  const one = unit { n: 1 }
  base() + twice(21) + step + one.n + origin()
}
